theory:
## Ensuring Type Safety

### Type Checking Pipeline

```
AST → Type Checker → Typed AST
  │
  ├── Type inference (deduce types from usage)
  ├── Type checking (verify declared types match)
  ├── Unification (solve type equations)
  ├── Constraint solving (resolve T: Ord constraints)
  └── Monomorphization (generate concrete code)
```

### Type Inference

```xiom
// Without type inference (explicit):
let x: Int = 42;
let y: Int = x + 1;

// With type inference:
let x = 42;       // Inferred: Int
let y = x + 1;    // Inferred: Int (from x: Int, + returns Int)
```

### Unification Algorithm

```xiom
// Type checker sees:
fn add[T](a: T, b: T) -> T { return a + b; }

// Call: add(1, 2)
// Unification:
//   T = Int   (from first argument)
//   T = Int   (from second argument, consistent!)
//   Returns: Int

// Call: add(1, "hello")
// Unification:
//   T = Int   (from first argument)
//   T = Str   (from second argument)
//   ERROR: type mismatch — cannot unify Int with Str
```

### Type Environment

```xiom
pub type TypeEnv = {
  variables: HashMap[Str, Type];
  functions: HashMap[Str, FunctionType];
  types: HashMap[Str, TypeDefinition];
  generics: Vec[GenericParam];
}

impl TypeEnv {
  fn lookup(self: &TypeEnv, name: &Str) -> Option[Type] {
    return self.variables.get(name);
  }

  fn unify(self: &mut TypeEnv, t1: Type, t2: Type) -> Result[(), TypeError] {
    return match (t1, t2) {
      (Type::Var(id1), Type::Var(id2)) if id1 == id2 => Ok(()),
      (Type::Var(id), other) if !occurs(id, other) => {
        self.substitutions.insert(id, other);
        Ok(())
      },
      (Type::Int, Type::Int) => Ok(()),
      (Type::Fn(args1, ret1), Type::Fn(args2, ret2)) => {
        self.unify_fn(args1, ret1, args2, ret2)
      },
      _ => Err(TypeError::Mismatch(t1, t2)),
    };
  }
}
```

### Common Type Errors

| Error | Cause | Fix |
|-------|-------|-----|
| Type mismatch | Int where Str expected | Check variable types |
| Cannot infer type | No type annotation, no usage | Add `:Type` annotation |
| Trait not satisfied | T doesn't implement required interface | Add constraint or impl |
| Recursive type | Type references itself without indirection | Add Box or reference |

